  "tip": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "hear 是常考感官动词，所以学生一定要掌握其习惯用法："
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1) hear sb. doing sth. 指动作正在进行当中。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "例如：I "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "hear him talking"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " next door. 我听到他正在隔壁房间讲话。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2) hear sb. do sth. 指动作已发生，完成了，也就是说听到整个过程。意思是“听到某人做了某事”，动作不再呈现。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "例如：Would you ask her to sing a song for us? We’d like to "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "hear her sing"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " like a soprano."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "你能让她为我们唱一首歌吗？我们喜欢听她像女高音那样唱。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "3) 大多数的感官动作（see, watch, notice 等）都可以用于这两种结构，但要注意加以区别。用 v-ing，表示动作正在进行，即处于发生的过程中，还没有结束；用不定式则表示全过程，或经常性的动作，或过去的动作。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "试比较：Do you "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "hear someone knocking"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " at the door?（讲时还在敲）"
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "I "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "heard someone knock"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " at the door three times.（讲时敲的动作已结束）"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
